# Phone number RTL / BiDi display

Under document RTL (Arabic), strings that start with `+` (E.164) are reordered by the Unicode BiDi algorithm unless isolated as LTR. That turns `+1 555-939-3585` into `555-939-3585 1+`.

## Required pattern

For any **displayed** phone / E.164 string in the UI, use `PhoneText` from `components/PhoneText.tsx` (also re-exported from `components/index`):

```tsx
import { PhoneText, isPhoneLike } from '../components/PhoneText';

<PhoneText>{lead.phone}</PhoneText>
{t('connected')} · <PhoneText>{phone}</PhoneText>
```

`PhoneText` sets `dir="ltr"` and `[unicode-bidi:isolate]` (same idea as Billing money islands).

## Ambiguous titles

When a label might be either a name or a phone (e.g. WhatsApp `account.name`, Messaging Center contact title), wrap only when phone-like:

```tsx
{isPhoneLike(title) ? (
  <PhoneText as="p" className="font-semibold ...">{title}</PhoneText>
) : (
  <p className="font-semibold ...">{title}</p>
)}
```

## Anti-patterns

- Do **not** render raw `{phone}`, `{phone_number}`, or phone-like `{account.name}` inside an RTL parent without `PhoneText`.
- `dir="ltr"` alone is weaker than isolate — prefer `PhoneText` for display text.
- Do **not** change `tel:` / `wa.me` / API payloads — only visible text needs isolation.
- Inputs: keep using `PhoneInput` (already `dir="ltr"`); do not wrap inputs in `PhoneText`.

## Related

- Lead phone rows: `LeadContactPhone` / `LeadContactPhoneList` (already BiDi-safe).
- Shared class tokens: `PHONE_TEXT_CLASS`, `PHONE_BIDI_CLASS` in `components/PhoneText.tsx`.
